body:
Every distributed agent template `opencode-suite/agents/*.md` carries opencode 2.x native frontmatter. opencode evaluates an agent's ordered `permissions` array of `{ action, resource, effect }` rules; it combines the rules in order with lower-priority configuration first, global rules appended next, and agent rules appended last, and the last matching rule wins (a different precedence diverges the fs-tool scope from the `edit` scope). The documented action vocabulary is opencode 2.x's — `read`, `edit`, `glob`, `grep`, `shell`, `subagent`, `skill`, `question`, `webfetch`, `websearch`, `external_directory`, and the apg-suite tool actions. The template's other native fields are `description`, `mode` (`primary` | `subagent` | `all`), `model` (a variant joins it as `provider/model#variant`), a Markdown body that becomes the agent's `system` prompt, and the display/limit fields `hidden`, `steps`, `color`, and `disabled`. A V2 agent definition carries zero of the legacy fields `temperature`, `top_p`, `prompt`, `permission`, `tools`, `disable`, and `maxSteps`. The distributed hidden subagents carry `hidden: true`, which removes an agent from normal listings and the subagent catalog — a visibility control; permissions restrict behaviour (`domain.entity.opencode-permission-rule-set`).

Each template's grant set:
- the `codebase-navigator` holds the `subagent`-action rules whose resource is the target agent ID — naming the distributed suite agents, the `*-implementer` agents, and the release-agent as dispatch targets — plus the apg-suite tool action rules;
- the `agent-builder` holds its main-checkout `edit` rules (`.opencode/agents/**`, `opencode.json`, `AGENTS.md`) and its exact read-only git verb set plus `git add`/`git commit` as `shell` rules;
- the `implementation-phase-reviewer` holds its read-only apg-suite, plan-read, and review rules, with the `question`/edit/scan/authoring rules absent (`domain.entity.distributed-agent-set`).

Acceptance criteria: every `opencode-suite/agents/*.md` file carries a `permissions` array whose entries name opencode 2.x actions and carry the agent's own grant set; each template enumerates its grant set so the set is checkable on its own; the `agent-builder.md` main-checkout `edit` rules and read-only git verb set are present; each template carries the V2-native fields (`description`, `mode`, `model`, the Markdown body as `system`, `permissions`, and any of `hidden`/`steps`/`color`/`disabled` it sets) and carries zero of the legacy fields `temperature`/`top_p`/`prompt`/`permission`/`tools`/`disable`/`maxSteps`; the hidden subagents carry `hidden: true`.
